<title>Australia: West Australia state threatened with trade sanctions.</title>
<headline>West Australia state threatened with trade sanctions.</headline>
<byline>Carolyn Simmonds</byline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trades union leaders warned on Wednesday that industrial action in Western Australia state over new labour relations laws could be stepped up and an appeal made to colleagues in Asia to impose international trade bans.</p>
<p>After a day of strikes which saw air links to the state cut on Tuesday, late-night talks between state premier Richard Court and Jenny George, president of the Australian Council of Trade Unions (ACTU), failed to resolve the dispute.</p>
</text>
